Your password has been changed.

It is shorter than $_arg_limit characters, which is accepted but worth
telling you about.

NIST SP 800-63B asks for at least $_arg_limit characters for a password
that is used on its own, and an fml administrator password is used on
its own -- there is no second factor behind it.

  https://pages.nist.gov/800-63-4/sp800-63b.html

The same document says a verifier "SHALL NOT impose other composition
rules (e.g., requiring mixtures of different character types)", so
nothing here asks you to add a digit or a symbol.  Length is what is
being asked for.

Please consider setting one of $_arg_limit characters or more.  Several
unrelated words joined together will get you there and is easier to
remember than a short string made deliberately awkward.
